<pagesize pagetype="Letter" orientation="portrait" width="8.500000" height="11.000000" units="in" page-scale="1.000000"/>
<section xid="1" props="page-margin-footer:0.5in; page-margin-header:0.5in">
<p style="Heading 1" xid="2"><c>Node JS backend</c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="3"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="4"><c>What is node JS<br/><br/></c><c props="font-weight:bold">WHAT</c><c> - Node.js is a runtime that lets you run javascript outside of the browser. </c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="7"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="8"><c props="font-weight:bold">WHY</c><c> - Node.js gives access to multple things that broswer cant do like- reading writting file, handling http request, talking directly to databse etc. </c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="9"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="11"><c>Node JS is event-driven and non blocking. <br/><br/>Means its perform multiple events and dont stop and keep wait for 1 event. node.js will keep executing code and as soon as event finished keep reacting to events. </c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="10"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="5"><c></c></p>
<p style="Normal" xid="6"><c></c></p>
</section>
